text:
The plate is a square dinner plate of about 26 cm. The items on it are dark, oval and glossy, and each is about 2.5-3 cm long. They look like Kalamata olives, probably pitted, though dates are the look-alike. The shine and the purple-brown color point to olives, so I went with olives.

I count about 12. A pitted Kalamata weighs roughly 4 g, so the total is about 12 × 4 = 48 g. Kalamata olives are about 115-140 kcal per 100 g, so I used 135.

